      "document_id": "a1152262daa2c2e9e30dc6b14a7917fa8e5d2b068757757dfc590f307a445834",
      "path": "docs/research/free-content/discovery/LANGUAGE_CULTURE_MEDIA.md",
      "line": 153,
      "heading": "C20 — Educational podcasts, lectures and documentaries",
      "text": "**Where to start.** Begin with universities, public educational broadcasters and\ninstitutional media producers, following their series/catalog links. In India,\n[NPTEL's course catalog](https://nptel.ac.in/courses) provides instructor/course\nand institutional discovery leads; investigate official educational broadcaster\nand university series alongside it. For international and US material, inspect\nuniversity lecture catalogs and public-media learning collections. The\n[Internet Archive developer portal](https://archive.org/developers/) documents\nmetadata tools for archive-hosted media; [Wikimedia Commons API guidance](https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Commons:API)\nsupports another metadata route, with license and exclusion markers to review.",
      "status": "historical-context-needs-reconciliation"
    }
  ]
}
